  "rationale": "No single step is a chokepoint, because every candidate has a working alternative path to crownData:exfiltrate. crownData is an OR of codeRepo, dbReplica, shareMount and vaultRead. codeRepo is an OR of monitoringHost and jumpHost. vaultRead depends on jumpHost. Blocking codeRepo still leaves vaultRead via jumpHost, which comes from dbLogin. Blocking jumpHost or vaultRead still leaves codeRepo via monitoringHost. monitoringHost is an OR of configSecret, ssoLogin and dbLogin, so blocking any one of these leaves the others. configSecret is an OR of the foothold vpnGateway and ciRunner, so it survives any single non-foothold block. Blocking mailClient, ciRunner or tokenCache still leaves configSecret, then monitoringHost, then codeRepo. Blocking monitoringHost still leaves jumpHost via dbLogin (mailClient AND configSecret), then vaultRead and codeRepo."
